                                                     1.2 Long-term accumulation of trace contaminants in
                                                     saline-alkaline water further exacerbates human
                                                     health risks

                                                         As a result of long-term human activities, groundwater salinization areas are often
                                                     accompanied by trace contaminants such as antibiotics, pesticides, heavy metals (e.g.,
                                                     arsenic and lead) and ﬂuoride. The long-term accumulation of these pollutants poses a
                                                     signiﬁcant threat to human health. The persistence of antibiotics can lead to the spread of
                                                     antibiotic resistance genes in groundwater and facilitate the dissemination of resistance. The
                                                     accumulation of drug-resistant pathogens is a direct threat to human health. It also disrupts the
                                                     microbial balance in ecosystems, which affects the natural puriﬁcation functions of soil and



